From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: a window out of sight keeps the slow refresh tick

What: while the window cannot be seen (hidden, minimised, wholly covered,
another Space, closed with "Keep running"), a frame kept for it is no work
for QEMU's refresh tick: the tick slows to 500 ms as on an idle desktop and
no longer asks for the present again on every tick. The frame is drawn when
the window shows again (omacvmWindowSeen schedules present_bh), as before.
qemu.log's "N frames not drawn" now counts frames, not ticks.

Why: omacvm-cocoa-present-unseen.patch keeps an unseen window's frame
dirty, and qemu-cocoa-idle-refresh.patch takes a dirty frame as work, so
once any frame came while the window was away the tick ran at the
display's rate for as long as it stayed away: on the Mac mini (60 Hz) QEMU
woke 142-151 times a second minimised against 88-94 with the window shown,
its main loop four times busier (idle-power track, round 4). On a 120 Hz
panel twice that.

Upstream: not sent (both patches are OmacVM's).
Test: app/runtime/Tests/display/test-idle-refresh-unseen.sh (the wiring in
the patched ui/cocoa.m, with --self-test in CI); QEMU's wakeups minimised
before and after (bench lock), the newest frame on screen at once after
unminimise, a Space switch and reopening a window closed with Keep running.
Applies after omacvm-cocoa-present-unseen.patch.

--- a/ui/cocoa.m
+++ b/ui/cocoa.m
@@ -7990,12 +7990,33 @@ - (void)tick:(CADisplayLink *)link
 
 static void cocoa_refresh_tick(bool pending);
 
+/*
+ * OmacVM: the window cannot be seen, so cocoa_gl_present keeps the frame
+ * (omacvm-cocoa-present-unseen.patch; OMACVM_PRESENT_HIDDEN=1 draws anyway).
+ */
+static bool omacvm_present_held(void)
+{
+    static int always = -1;
+
+    if (always < 0) {
+        always = getenv("OMACVM_PRESENT_HIDDEN") != NULL;
+    }
+    return present_ctx && !qatomic_read(&omacvm_window_seen) && !always;
+}
+
 static void cocoa_gl_refresh(DisplayChangeListener *dcl)
 {
+    /*
+     * OmacVM: a frame kept for a window out of sight is no work for the
+     * tick. It is drawn when the window shows again (omacvmWindowSeen ->
+     * present_bh), not tried again on every tick at the display's rate.
+     */
+    bool held = omacvm_present_held();
+
     cocoa_refresh(dcl);
-    cocoa_refresh_tick(gl_dirty);
+    cocoa_refresh_tick(gl_dirty && !held);
 
-    if (gl_dirty) {
+    if (gl_dirty && !held) {
 
         if (cocoa_gl_trace_enabled()) {
             cocoa_gl_log("refresh: triggering render dirty scanout=%d egl_surface=%d",
